      },
      "text": "Days 3–6: Jungle and wildlife watching"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_title:8fa505c430bf2bb8",
      "field": "itinerary.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "1a905ada23e822870b032a8cca6328c91374184954584bdd048d58ca2d84a434",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw9pzpme-g1f7fnp0wz",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Days 3–6: Jungle and wildlife watching"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "596473bd1dcc93442de1783563ede61e9c47a76f24e8a85bbb09e1a9b8c25a43",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw9pzpme-g1f7fnp0wz",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "The flight to Kabalebo Nature Resort takes about 75 minutes. On arrival, settle into a clean, comfortable lodge in the Amazon rainforest.\n\nOver the next few days, explore the jungle on walks and hikes, take boat trips on the river, watch for wildlife and birds, and go climbing, swimming or kayaking. You can also relax in the river rapids, where the flowing water provides a natural massage, and take in the rainforest views.\n\nOne of the more unusual outings is a night walk in the jungle with an experienced guide. You may also see an ocelot that visits the lodge.\n\nOn the fourth day of this part of the trip, return to Paramaribo and check in to your hotel.\n\nMeals: breakfast, lunch and dinner."
